// such as a SUriClip, but you only want it to create a subset of these types,
// you should set the SClip:supported-formats of the clip to the subset of
// types. This should be done *before* adding the clip to a layer.
//
// If a clip will produce several core elements of the same
// STrackElement:track-type, you should connect to the timeline's
// STimeline::select-tracks-for-object signal to coordinate which tracks each
// element should land in. Note, no two core children within a clip can share
// the same STrack, so you should not select the same track for two separate
// core children. Provided you stick to this rule, it is still safe to select
// several tracks for the same core child, the core child will be copied into
// the additional tracks. You can manually add the child to more tracks later
// using ges_clip_add_child_to_track(). If you do not wish to use a core child,
// you can always select no track.
//
// The STimelineElement:in-point of the clip will control the
// STimelineElement:in-point of its core children to be the same value if their
// STrackElement:has-internal-source is set to TRUE.
//
// The STimelineElement:max-duration of the clip is the minimum
// STimelineElement:max-duration of its core children. If you set its
// value to anything other than its current value, this will also set
// the STimelineElement:max-duration of all its core children to the
// same value if their STrackElement:has-internal-source is set to TRUE.
